umongous fan of the office i've  watched a show  like i think 50 000 times but you know i  still laugh every day  if we watch that so um you know we watch  things like that  and and um you know i have so many  friends that  um you know would make me laugh and and  and  things like that and sarah also made me  laugh all the time so you you need that  whenever you're going through this  uh are you cancer-free like what's your  diagnosis as far as follow-ups go  yeah so i mean everything looks  fantastic  so far but after you have stage three  colon cancer go through chemotherapy you  go through about a five year  surveillance period  where um for the first year every three  months you get checked up  and then the next year it's every six  months and then it's yearly for the next  three years after that so  um i'm getting checked up again in  september  and then after that it progresses to six  months so you get uh  ct scans and then i have really highly  specific blood tests that i do too and  so far everything looks great i feel  great about everything and  and my future but it's still something  that you have to deal with even after  it's over  what if i got you an autographed picture  from uh kevin from the office  would you uh would you be interested in  getting i actually noticed  his uh mug in front of you i would love  that  yeah i'm a huge fan well plus when he  spills the chili i mean they're  one of the best and that's that's that  was one take he said that he did it one  time that was it  and they had to replace the carpet as he  spilled all the uh the chili  but it's still if i'm ever in a bad mood  and if i'm feeling low you can watch  that and i don't care what you're going  through you can feel a little bit better  single time yeah that would have been  tough if it was more than one take that  would have been uh  pretty tough so i'm happy for him that  it was only one take  uh are you okay with uh baseball  changing the rules no more  seven inning uh double headers here and  uh we're getting rid of the guy on  second base  to start extra innings um you know what  as a player i  i haven't minded the rules too much uh  the seven ending double headers are  uh nice two nine inning games in a day  is a lot but  at the same time um you know that is a  classic baseball game and and  um so so i have no problem with it  changing back but i have not minded the  change in rules either  uh did any pitcher take it easy on you  did anybody  want to just you know give you a  meatball down the down the middle  most definitely not uh yeah they  if they did i i i wouldn't be too happy  with them uh as nice as that sounds  you know i i don't want any sympathy or  uh you know courtesy meatballs from  anybody else and i know  uh the pictures this year i feel like  are almost more than any other year  they're just getting better and better  and they know how to pitch and  um yeah it's tough it's it's tough on a  day-to-day basis going out there and  facing these guys  are you doing a website or anything i  know you want to raise awareness here  i'm curious if you and your girlfriend  or your agent have started something yes  so i have a foundation it's called the  trey mancini foundation  and so my older sister actually is the  one that started it my younger sister  helps out and sarah helps out and my  agent is also involved and  um you know a lot of what we do is to  benefit  colon cancer and raise awareness but we  also do a backpack program in baltimore  to benefit  kids up there so basically anything that  resonates with us we want to get behind  and we do a lot of different fundraisers  for different causes but right now our  main things are colon cancer awareness  and the backpack program  great to talk to you trey and uh i know  you want to be known as a ball player  but you know what if you can raise any  kind of awareness  uh there's nothing wrong with being  known as that ball player who helped  a lot of people and maybe save some  lives absolutely yeah i  really appreciate it dan thanks for  having me on that's uh trey mancini the  oil's first baseman  and uh finished runner-up home run derby  to uh pete alonso


